        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin Bacon, Lawrence Turman, Curtis Hanson, Meryl Streep, David Strathairn, John C. Reilly, Benjamin Bratt, Joseph Mazzello, Lucie Arnaz, Craig Wasson, Ken Howard, Anne Schedeen\n- Films: The River Wild, Footloose, JFK, A Few Good Men, Apollo 13, Mystic River, Pretty Poison, The Great White Hope, The Thing, Mass Appeal, Short Circuit, American History X, Second Thoughts\n- Roles: actor, musician, director, producer\n\nFacts:\n- Lawrence Turman directed the 1983 American drama film Second Thoughts, which starred Lucie Arnaz, Craig Wasson, Ken Howard, and Anne Schedeen.\n- Kevin Bacon is an American actor and musician who was born on July 8, 1958.\n- Kevin Bacon's notable films include Footloose (1984), JFK (1991), A Few Good Men (1992), Apollo 13 (1995), and Mystic River (2003).\n- The River Wild is a 1994 American adventure crime-thriller film directed by Curtis Hanson and starring Meryl Streep, Kevin Bacon, David Strathairn, John C. Reilly, Benjamin Bratt, and Joseph Mazzello as Roarke.\n- Lawrence Turman produced Pretty Poison (1968), The Great White Hope (1970), The Thing (1982), Mass Appeal (1984), Short Circuit (1986), The River Wild (1994), and American History X (1998).",
